# Maps

• **Source of Truth** - always represents actual idea
• [This instance maps index](instance/maps/index.md)
• Each map: `instance/maps/{name}/` — YAML, scripts, `Readme.md` (how to read / apply)
• Maps store **secret's keys** , not values. Secrets: `instance/{app}/.env` (OIDC: `.env.oidc`). Domains: `instance/caddy/.env`
• Do not curl, use apply, dump... scripts & app's specfic scripts

# Scripts

• Scripts **NEVER DELETE DATA**: only create/update
Do not add `--delete` to map scripts - all deletion manualy after "Aprove Deletion Workflow"
• Scripts **indepetent**: any time scripts called produces same result as described in a map
• Keep scripts in map's folder (right to the map)

# AI

• AI can delete only after aprove granted by a user

## Aprove Deletion Workflow

0. Read related applications actual data (to check is there any other data different from application's map)
1. Create laconic `todo/deletion-list.md` - list of all permissions, groups and other data from the maps
Separate Differences in first section (if found in `step 0`)

2. **Explicitly** asks the user to delete data - wait for user's aprove for deletion
Present 2 questions: 1) delete found differences (only if found any)? 2) aprove deletion of the `todo/deletion-list.md`

3. Implement what user answers - manualy, be carefull **dont broke anything**
User can will specify exactly what do to; he can ask to sync found differences (or only part of them)

### Update Map Workflow

0. Read related applications actual data (to check is there any other data different from application's map)
1. Edit the YAML (right file).
YAML doesnt store secrets; it points to `instance/{app}/.env` values, by property names.